# Apex Logics — redirect table (Apache 2.4 / DreamHost)
# Repo-managed per AL-REDIRECTS. This file deploys via the existing rsync
# pipeline (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) and is NOT in the rsync exclude
# list, so it ships on every push. --delete is active on that rsync, so this
# repo copy is the only source of truth — do not hand-edit on the server,
# it will be destroyed on the next deploy.
#
# Rules: Redirect 301 only (permanent — transfers search authority).
# One rule per line, dated, attributed to the WU that caused it.
# No RewriteEngine, no security headers, no caching rules here — see
# AL-REDIRECTS-SPEC.md §2 for scope boundaries. Log of what's live: REDIRECTS.md.
#
# 2026-07-27 (AL-REDIRECTS survey): no rule entries yet. Audited candidates —
# AL-58/AL-60 never shipped (no live URL ever existed); AL-06+16 and AL-08+14
# were combined before their individual tool pages ever went live (no old
# URLs to redirect); the AL-AP2PROSE slug rename referenced in the spec did
# not happen (ap2-advisor-prompt-composer is still the live slug). See
# REDIRECTS.md for the full audit trail. Renaming or retiring a tool going
# forward REQUIRES a Redirect 301 entry below — see repo/CLAUDE.md.
